.TH HELLXCB 1 hellxcb
.SH NAME
hellxcb \- minimal and dynamic tiling window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hellxcb 
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
hellxcb is a very minimal, lightweight, tiny but monsterous, dynamic tiling
window manager with floating mode support. It will try to stay as small as
possible.
.P
.SH MODES
It allows the "normal" method of tiling window managers (with the new window as
the master) and with the new window opened at the bottom of the stack
.P
.B hellxcb
has three other modes:
.I Bottom stack
where the slave clients (the smaller "windows") are tiled beneath the master.
.I Grid mode
where the windows are divided equally into a grid.
.I Floating mode
where windows keep the place and size they ask for, and can be moved and
resized freely. A window moved or resized with the mouse in a tiling mode
floats until its tiling mode is selected again or the modes are cycled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
prints a usage line to standard error, then exits.
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to standard error, then exits.
.SH USAGE
.SS Status bar
hellxcb does not provide a status bar. Consistent with the Unix philosophy,
hellxcb provides information to the status bar or panel of choice via text.
Whenever the desktop, the mode or the windows change, it writes one line to
the file HELLXCB_TAG_AND_MODE in
.I config.h
(default
.IR /tmp/hellxcb.txt ),
for example:
.P
.nf
[tag: 1] [mode: tile] [windows: 2] [tag 1 win: 2] [tag 2 win: 0] [tag 3 win: 1] [tag 4 win: 0]
.fi
.P
That is the current desktop, its mode (tile, bstack, grid or float), its number
of windows, and the number of windows on every desktop. The drop-down terminal
is not counted.
.SS Keyboard and mouse commands
All of
.I hellxcb's
commands can be customized by editing
.I config.h
and recompiling. The default key-bindings include:
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-Return
Start
.BR xterm (1).
.TP
.B Mod4\-v
Start
.BR dmenu (1).
.TP
.B Mod4\-z
Show or hide the drop-down terminal; the first press starts it. Its command,
width and height are set in
.IR config.h .
.TP
.B Mod1\-b
Toggles the panel on and off.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-t
Sets tiled layout.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-b
Sets bottom stack layout.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-g
Sets grid layout.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-f
Sets floating layout: windows keep the place and size they ask for.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-y
Cycle through all layouts.
.TP
.B Mod1\-j
Focus next window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-k
Focus previous window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-j
Move the focussed window down the stack.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-k
Move the focussed window up the stack.
.TP
.B Mod1\-l
Increase master area size.
.TP
.B Mod1\-h
Decrease master area size.
.TP
.B Mod1\-p
Grow the first stack window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-o
Shrink the first stack window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Return
Swaps the focused window to/from master area (tiled layouts only).
.TP
.B Mod1\-Backspace
Focus the window that raised an urgent hint. If no such window in current desktop,
search other desktops, and focus the desktop and window that raised the urgent hint.
.TP
.B Mod1\-c
Close focused window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-{1..4}
Move to the nth desktop. By default,
.I hellxcb
is configured with four desktops.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-{1..4}
Move focused window to the nth desktop.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Control\-{h,l}
Move to the previous/next desktop.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Shift\-{h,l}
Move to the previous/next desktop that has windows.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Tab
Toggles to the last selected desktop.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Control\-r
Quit hellxcb with exit status 0.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Control\-q
Quit hellxcb with exit status 1. A loop in
.I .xinitrc
can use the two exit statuses to tell a restart from a quit.
.TP
.B Mod1\-m
Move the mouse pointer to the rightmost screen edge.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button1
Dragging the mouse will move the selected window and make it float.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button3
Dragging the mouse will resize the selected window and make it float.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
will bring up
.I dmenu
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.I hellxcb
is customized by editing
.I config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1)
.SH BUGS
.I hellxcb
is under active development. Please report all bugs to the author.
